Photovoltaic technology solid-state physics par based hoti hai aur remote areas mein clean energy provide karti hai.

• Option A is Incorrect because solar cells mechanical turbine generators par rely nahi karte aur inme koi rotational friction nahi hota.

• Option B is Correct because **Solar (Photovoltaic) Cells** ke main operational advantages hain:
- **Solid-State Reliability**: Inme **koi moving mechanical parts nahi hote**, jisse friction wear-and-tear eliminate ho jata hai;
- **Low Maintenance**: Bohot minimal servicing require hoti hai aur operational lifespan 20-25 years se zyada hota hai;
- **Diffuse Light Utilization**: Ye regular sunlight ke under bina complex optical focusing mirrors ya mechanical tracking ke operate karte hain;
- **Decentralized Deployment**: Inhe remote ya inaccessible areas (jaise artificial satellites, space stations, remote lighthouses aur villages) mein easily install kiya ja sakta hai jahan transmission grid lines bichhana economically unfeasible hota hai.

• Option C is Incorrect because solar cells ko operate karne ke liye kisi natural gas combustion ki zaroorat nahi hoti.

• Option D is Incorrect because solar cells operation ke dauran zero greenhouse gas emission produce karte hain.

Bio-gas agricultural aur organic animal waste se obtain hone wala ek efficient aur eco-friendly domestic fuel alternative hai.

• Option A is Incorrect because indoor smoke aur particulate matter air pollution generate karte hain aur ye koi advantage nahi hai.

• Option B is Correct because **Bio-gas** wood, dried cow-dung cakes ya coal burn karne ke mukable clear environmental, economic aur domestic advantages offer karta hai:
- **Smokeless Blue Flame**: Harmful particulate matter emit kiye bina cleanly burn hota hai, indoor respiratory diseases ko prevent karta hai;
- **Zero Solid Residue**: Piche koi unburnt soot ya ash nahi chhodta, household cleaning burdens ko eliminate karta hai;
- **High Energy Output**: Up to $75\%$ methane contain karta hai, providing high calorific value;
- **Sanitation and Organic Manure**: Animal dung aur organic wastes ko hygienically dispose karta hai while converting them into nutrient-rich organic nitrogen/phosphorus fertilizer.

• Option C is Incorrect because biogas deforestation ko badhava nahi deta balki fuelwood dependency kam karke forests bachata hai.

• Option D is Incorrect because biogas ki spent slurry soil ko nitrogen aur phosphorus se enrich karti hai na ki deplete.

Large-scale commercial wind farms clean energy produce karte hain lekin unke sath specific spatial aur local atmospheric limitations judi hoti hain.

• Option A is Incorrect because ozone depletion stratosphere mein chemical CFCs se hota hai, mechanical turbine blades se nahi.

• Option B is Correct because operation ke dauran wind energy renewable aur non-polluting hone ke bawajood, **large-scale commercial wind farms distinct physical aur environmental limitations face karte hain**:
- **Enormous Land Footprint**: Approx **$2\text{ hectares of open land per 1 MW}$** generation capacity require hoti hai;
- **Micro-climatic Alteration**: Massive turbine blades ke dense arrays local aerodynamic wind velocities aur boundary layer moisture circulation ko alter karte hain, potentially **local rainfall aur weather patterns ko disturb** kar sakte hain;
- **High Capital and Weathering Costs**: Rotating components cyclonic winds, rain aur salt corrosion ke continuous exposure mein rehte hain;
- **Avian Hazard**: Migratory bird populations ke liye collision hazards pose karte hain.

• Option C is Incorrect because wind turbines me fossil fuels burn nahi hote, isliye sulfur dioxide ya acid rain ka question hi nahi uthta.

• Option D is Incorrect because wind generation groundwater hydrology ko deplete nahi karta.
